# Design: Responsive documentation hero

## Problem
PR #113 expanded the canonical homepage description for answer-engine visibility. The fixed 188px logo remained side-by-side with the longer copy at mobile widths, so bottom alignment pushed the logo down and squeezed the text.

## Approach
Stack the existing logo above full-width copy below the small breakpoint, while preserving the desktop row and the canonical SEO/AEO wording verbatim. Add responsive padding and min-width protection without changing metadata or content.

## Key Trade-offs
- Preserve the visible canonical identity sentence instead of shortening or hiding it.
- Accept a taller mobile hero in exchange for readable copy and stable logo placement.

